doc: domain.hick
83e1|<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
35bf|<hick:doc xmlns:hick="http://www.hickorydocs.com/1.0" weave="domain.md">
d159|# Todo app — domain model
f011|
ce0d|<hick:upstream file="meetings/2026-08-07-kickoff.hick" />
f011|
5a37|The vocabulary. Terms are tagged `.glossary` so downstream documents can pull
dc66|the whole set by class. Decisions are NOT restated here — they arrive from the
80b2|meeting by reference, so each is written down in exactly one place and every
539b|document below this one goes stale together when it changes.
f011|
02f5|## Terms
f011|
3f79|<hick:copy id="t-task" class="glossary">
3e6f|**Task** — one thing to do. Has an id, a title, and a state. Nothing else;
c5e0|every field anyone proposed beyond these was left as an open question.
ae0e|</hick:copy>
f011|
e00f|<hick:copy id="t-state" class="glossary">
96c7|**State** — which of open, done, or dropped a task is in. Exactly one at a
3fa6|time; there is no "partially done".
ae0e|</hick:copy>
f011|
bd0c|<hick:copy id="t-dropped" class="glossary">
ed0c|**Dropped** — decided against, deliberately retained. Distinct from deleted,
f905|which the app does not offer. Dropping is a decision worth keeping a record
2b4d|of.
ae0e|</hick:copy>
f011|
7d9c|<hick:copy id="t-list" class="glossary">
0826|**List** — the whole set of tasks, in creation order. There is one list; the
37b3|app has no concept of multiple lists or projects.
ae0e|</hick:copy>
f011|
43df|## Decisions this model rests on
f011|
dff3|<hick:paste select=".decision" />
f011|
505c|## Why dropped is not deleted
f011|
5a6b|The state decision above is the one that shapes the data model. A deleted
509e|task leaves no trace, so "why isn't this in the list any more" has no answer.
f064|A dropped task answers it. That costs nothing here — the file keeps every
a41e|task regardless — and it is the difference between a log and a list.
de5c|</hick:doc>

